   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.2. Increased institutional capacity of workers&#x2019; organizations</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2022-23, the Arab Trade Union Confederation (ATUC) enhanced its institutional capacities to support its affiliate entities in defending the rights and interests of all workers, including migrant workers, through the development and the adoption of trade union policies and strategies on fair migration, based on the ILO Fair Recruitment Initiative Strategy 2021-2025, International Labour Standards (ILS) , and other relevant ILO documents.

In 2022-23, the ATUC enhanced its institutional capacities to influence just transition policies through the development and adoption of an Arab Trade Union policy action on Just transition, national trade union strategies to organize and defend workers in the informal economy.	 Via the Regular Budget funds, the ILO supported the Arab Trade Union Confederation (ATUC) to hold four parallel side events during its 3rd congress that took place in Oran, Algeria on 13-16 September 2022 on Just Transition, Fair Recruitment, Unions in Transition, and workers in informality.</narrative>
   </description>
